We can creates multiple routers in a single controller 
we also have options to perform server side validations
we can also perform query like filtering based on certain property
we shouldnt use models for everything, instead we have to use Data Transfer Object to send or recieve Data
We must follow a proper principle to design and we must perform operations with the classes that it is meant to be used as
We have Controller,Repository,Services

Inside we define all the controllers which are reponsible http requests
    -Get,post,Put,Delete..
    -We can extract the data inside the routes using {name}
    -We have to build controller dependency using Builder

Model
    -We define all the properties in the models
    -We use anotations for server side validations but it is not a good practise to perform validations using models itself
    -models must be only used as a model and nothing else

Data transfer Object
    -We are not using models right
    -When we want to send data or recieve data we must maintain abstraction and that is the reason we are using DTO
    -Lets say we want to send userdetails but if we use model to send the user details then there id a problem of sending password along with it and we dont want that to happen
    To send the data and while recieving the data or to perform the opertaions with the data we must maintain a level of abstraction and this done using DTO

Mappers
    -We use mapper to convert one object to another object
    -lets say we have DTO to recieve the user details but we cant directly store DTO in database
    -We have to convert these DTO to models and then store them in the database.
    -Mapper are really helpfull in this scenario

Query
    -We can also perform query and retrieve the data right
    -We do that using query
    -inorder to perform query we need to create a query object and within that we write the property which can be used to fetch the data-in short we are performing filering
    -We also use [FromQuery] in as a parameter to do this and initialise a query object
    -these properties are optional

Repository
    -These are reponsible for performing operations with the database
    -We define an interface and then write down the methods 
    -we always use interface as a reference
    -this is a good practise to follow
    -We also have to provide various level of abstraction and make the code very flexible 
    -we will learn more about this when we do System design

Pagination
    -Lets say we have more than 10000 records and we have to retrive them
    -If we try to retrieve them seperatly then our app would actually crash
    -And that why we will use Pagination
    -We will divide them to pages
    
